{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 998244353L;\n\n    static long add(long x, long y) {\n        return ((x + y) % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    static long mult(long x, long y) {\n        return ((x * y) % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    static long exp(long x, long y) {\n        long res = 1;\n        while (y > 0) {\n            if (y % 2 == 1) res = mult(res, x);\n            x = mult(x, x);\n            y /= 2;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static long inv(long x) {\n        return exp(x, MOD - 2);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long m = sc.nextLong();\n        int k = sc.nextInt();\n\n        long[] dp = new long[k + 1];\n        dp[0] = 1;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            for (int j = k; j >= 0; j--) {\n                long fromPrevious = (j == 0) ? 0 : mult(dp[j - 1], n - (j - 1));\n                long fromSame = (j == k) ? 0 : mult(dp[j], j);\n                dp[j] = add(fromPrevious, fromSame);\n            }\n        }\n\n        long invM = inv(m);\n        long ans = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n            ans = add(ans, mult(dp[i], exp(invM, i)));\n        }\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 998244353LL;\n\nlong long add(long long x, long long y) {\n    return ((x + y) % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n}\n\nlong long mult(long long x, long long y) {\n    return ((x * y) % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n}\n\nlong long exp(long long x, long long y) {\n    long long res = 1;\n    while (y > 0) {\n        if (y % 2 == 1) res = mult(res, x);\n        x = mult(x, x);\n        y /= 2;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nlong long inv(long long x) {\n    return exp(x, MOD - 2);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n, m;\n    int k;\n    cin >> n >> m >> k;\n\n    vector<long long> dp(k + 1, 0);\n    dp[0] = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        for (int j = k; j >= 0; j--) {\n            long long fromPrevious = (j == 0) ? 0 : mult(dp[j - 1], n - (j - 1));\n            long long fromSame = (j == k) ? 0 : mult(dp[j], j);\n            dp[j] = add(fromPrevious, fromSame);\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long invM = inv(m);\n    long long ans = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n        ans = add(ans, mult(dp[i], exp(invM, i)));\n    }\n    cout << ans << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.843663479434326e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00014256415306590497, -1.764281842042692e-05, -1.8000440832111053e-05, -0.062022965401411057, -0.0005598884890787303, -0.03807492181658745, 0.0, -0.00044288364006206393, -0.3132910132408142, -0.06203741580247879, -4.768360213347478e-06, 0.0, -0.02975805476307869, -0.03912748396396637, -5.722029527532868e-06, -2.38418550679